I commented on and closed one issue, #1053, and left the other 11 alone because this session made no progress on them.

#1053 (closed): fixed in b4bd5438. The session wrap-up still has to push it.
• The fix: read_for_rewrite now starts from an empty file only when the file doesn't exist. Any other read error, such as invalid UTF-8 or permission denied, refuses the write, names the file and says nothing was written.
• `/todo board evidence`: this is where the issue was found. It now goes through read_for_rewrite, so an unreadable evidence.md gets a red refusal and isn't overwritten.
• Two more writers: the two /config set writers already used read_for_rewrite, so the same fix covers them. Before the fix, a .yoyo.toml with one 0xe9 byte was rewritten and the call reported success. So the bug had three instances, not the one the issue counted.
• Tests: three new tests, including one that checks an unreadable evidence.md keeps its original bytes. Putting the old code back fails exactly those three.

